.)\n\nThis adds comprehensive support for S3-compatible storage providers\nbeyond AWS S3, including Cloudflare R2, MinIO, DigitalOcean Spaces,\nBackblaze B2, and Wasabi.\n\nChanges to module/s3proxy.go:\n- Add ''endpoint'' configuration for custom S3 endpoints\n- Add ''use_path_style'' for path-style addressing (required for MinIO)\n- Add ''access_key_id'' and ''secret_access_key'' for inline credentials\n- Update Provision() to support custom endpoints and credentials\n- Add static credentials provider alongside default credential chain\n- Enhanced logging to show endpoint configuration\n\nNew Caddyfile directive options:\n- endpoint: Custom S3 endpoint URL\n- use_path_style: Force path-style addressing (bucket/path)\n- access_key_id: Access key for authentication\n- secret_access_key: Secret key for authentication\n\nCaddyfile.example additions:\n- Cloudflare R2 configuration with account ID endpoint\n- MinIO self-hosted storage example\n- DigitalOcean Spaces configuration\n- Backblaze B2 S3 API example\n- Wasabi Hot Cloud Storage example\n- Mixed storage example (AWS S3 + Cloudflare R2)\n- Updated configuration notes with S3-compatible providers\n- Security best practices for credential management\n\nDocumentation updates:\n- Add S3-compatible storage section to README\n- Add configuration examples for R2, MinIO, DigitalOcean Spaces\n- Update directive options table with new parameters\n- Update authentication section for S3-compatible storage\n- Update FAQ with R2 and S3-compatible storage questions\n- Add feature highlight for S3-compatible storage support\n\nBenefits:\n- Use Cloudflare R2 for zero egress fees\n- Self-host with MinIO for complete control\n- Mix different storage providers in same deployment\n- Lower costs with alternative providers\n- Support for air-gapped deployments with MinIO\n\nThis maintains full backward compatibility with existing AWS S3\nconfigurations while enabling flexible storage options.","tree":{"sha":"f6ef7a1dfcc09fb33fa4fd9b6460e0a20c0296b2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ibkrm/object-gate/git/trees/f6ef7a1dfcc09fb33fa4fd9b6460e0a20c0296b2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ibkrm/object-gate/git/commits/267f2918f22ee14cc65fcf5f3fe923d4a545dcc9","verification":{"payload":"tree f6ef7a1dfcc09fb33fa4fd9b6460e0a20c0296b2\nparent 5c51f56a8e4e1cad95f73d0214772b95686c1f67\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1763325658 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1763325658 +0000\n\nAdd support for S3-compatible storage (Cloudflare R2, MinIO, etc.)\n\nThis adds comprehensive support for S3-compatible storage providers\nbeyond AWS S3, including Cloudflare R2, MinIO, DigitalOcean Spaces,\nBackblaze B2, and Wasabi.\n\nChanges to module/s3proxy.go:\n- Add ''endpoint'' configuration for custom S3 endpoints\n- Add ''use_path_style'' for path-style addressing (required for MinIO)\n- Add ''access_key_id'' and ''secret_access_key'' for inline credentials\n- Update Provision() to support custom endpoints and credentials\n- Add static credentials provider alongside default credential chain\n- Enhanced logging to show endpoint configuration\n\nNew Caddyfile directive options:\n- endpoint: Custom S3 endpoint URL\n- use_path_style: Force path-style addressing (bucket/path)\n- access_key_id: Access key for authentication\n- secret_access_key: Secret key for authentication\n\nCaddyfile.example additions:\n- Cloudflare R2 configuration with account ID endpoint\n- MinIO self-hosted storage example\n- DigitalOcean Spaces configuration\n- Backblaze B2 S3 API example\n- Wasabi Hot Cloud Storage example\n- Mixed storage example (AWS S3 + Cloudflare R2)\n- Updated configuration notes with S3-compatible providers\n- Security best practices for credential management\n\nDocumentation updates:\n- Add S3-compatible storage section to README\n- Add configuration examples for R2, MinIO, DigitalOcean Spaces\n- Update directive options table with new parameters\n- Update authentication section for S3-compatible storage\n- Update FAQ with R2 and S3-compatible storage questions\n- Add feature highlight for S3-compatible storage support\n\nBenefits:\n- Use Cloudflare R2 for zero egress fees\n- Self-host with MinIO for complete control\n- Mix different storage providers in same deployment\n- Lower costs with alternative providers\n- Support for air-gapped deployments with MinIO\n\nThis maintains full backward compatibility with existing AWS S3\nconfigurations while enabling flexible storage options.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQGpuy7bR\n1yRwKS5Yr8Equ9cN7Zrw1GdpjtDVLdfBbp+/qfDSOkKkZxM7JERn6yTLR3FG3HR+z/fbvsU8DJYq\nDQs=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2025-11-16T20:41:08Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ibkrm/object-gate/commit/267f2918f22ee14cc65fcf5f3fe923d4a545dcc9","node_id":"C_kwDOQWQ7aNoAKDI2N2YyOTE4ZjIyZWUxNGNjNjVmY2Y1ZjNmZTkyM2Q0YTU0NWRjYzk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ibkrm/object-gate/commit/5c51f56a8e4e1cad95f73d0214772b95686c1f67","sha":"5c51f56a8e4e1cad95f73d0214772b95686c1f67","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ibkrm/object-gate/commits/5c51f56a8e4e1cad95f73d0214772b95686c1f67"}],"sha":"267f2918f22ee14cc65fcf5f3fe923d4a545dcc9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ibkrm/object-gate/commits/267f2918f22ee14cc65fcf5f3fe923d4a545dcc9"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ibkrm/object-gate/commits/5c51f56a8e4e1cad95f73d0214772b95686c1f67/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2025-11-16T19:08:58Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2025-11-16T19:08:58Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Implement S3 reverse proxy using Caddy module in Go\n\nThis implements a high-performance reverse proxy for serving static files\nfrom private AWS S3 buckets using a custom Caddy module written in Go.\n\nFeatures:\n- Host-based routing: Route different domains to different S3 paths\n- Path-based routing: Serve multiple apps from paths on same domain\n- SPA support: Automatic fallback to index.html for client-side routing\n- Hot reload: Zero-downtime configuration updates via Caddy Admin API\n- Private S3 buckets: No need to make buckets public\n- High performance: Built on Caddy/Go instead of Node.js\n- Docker support: Multi-stage build with Docker Compose\n\nArchitecture:\n- Custom Caddy module (http.handlers.s3_proxy)\n- AWS SDK Go v2 for S3 integration\n- Streaming: Files streamed directly from S3 to client\n- HTTP caching: ETag, Last-Modified, Cache-Control support\n\nComponents:\n- cmd/caddy/main.go: Custom Caddy binary entry point\n- module/s3proxy.go: S3 proxy Caddy module implementation\n- Caddyfile.example: Comprehensive configuration examples\n- Dockerfile: Multi-stage build for production\n- docker-compose.yml: Complete deployment setup\n- Makefile: Build, run, and development commands\n\nDocumentation:\n- README.md: Complete setup and usage guide\n- ARCHITECTURE.md: Technical design and implementation details\n- CONTRIBUTING.md: Development and contribution guidelines\n\nThis solution provides a flexible, performant alternative to CloudFront\nand API Gateway for serving static files from private S3 buckets with\ndynamic routing requirements.","tree":{"sha":"1c889a663cc4785b119b7defb07418e7f65388ae","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ibkrm/object-gate/git/trees/1c889a663cc4785b119b7defb07418e7f65388ae"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ibkrm/object-gate/git/commits/5c51f56a8e4e1cad95f73d0214772b95686c1f67","verification":{"payload":"tree 1c889a663cc4785b119b7defb07418e7f65388ae\nparent 2978f773d469249f4b13a0eef7df94d2b827ddbb\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1763320138 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1763320138 +0000\n\nImplement S3 reverse proxy using Caddy module in Go\n\nThis implements a high-performance reverse proxy for serving static files\nfrom private AWS S3 buckets using a custom Caddy module written in Go.\n\nFeatures:\n- Host-based routing: Route different domains to different S3 paths\n- Path-based routing: Serve multiple apps from paths on same domain\n- SPA support: Automatic fallback to index.html for client-side routing\n- Hot reload: Zero-downtime configuration updates via Caddy Admin API\n- Private S3 buckets: No need to make buckets public\n- High performance: Built on Caddy/Go instead of Node.js\n- Docker support: Multi-stage build with Docker Compose\n\nArchitecture:\n- Custom Caddy module (http.handlers.s3_proxy)\n- AWS SDK Go v2 for S3 integration\n- Streaming: Files streamed directly from S3 to client\n- HTTP caching: ETag, Last-Modified, Cache-Control support\n\nComponents:\n- cmd/caddy/main.go: Custom Caddy binary entry point\n- module/s3proxy.go: S3 proxy Caddy module implementation\n- Caddyfile.example: Comprehensive configuration examples\n- Dockerfile: Multi-stage build for production\n- docker-compose.yml: Complete deployment setup\n- Makefile: Build, run, and development commands\n\nDocumentation:\n- README.md: Complete setup and usage guide\n- ARCHITECTURE.md: Technical design and implementation details\n- CONTRIBUTING.md: Development and contribution guidelines\n\nThis solution provides a flexible, performant alternative to CloudFront\nand API Gateway for serving static files from private S3 buckets with\ndynamic routing requirements.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQNPnYquW\nMB41Dhkoa9kYecQIGMnB6AlbYqL1LSObT75TwcDsabGVXkGmjTLiuyxhF/Dz8jp2gDNxAmGQX82t\n6QM=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2025-11-16T19:09:07Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url