ubscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/p-hoffmann/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/p-hoffmann","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OHDSI/Atlas3/commits/ce85402467a4b972e25e4e84f377e864c3ea31c6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-21T18:12:37Z","email":"954078+p-hoffmann@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Peter Hoffmann"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-21T18:12:37Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Let the cohort and analysis lists be sorted by column (#280)\n\nThe cohort list was a hand written table whose headers were plain text,\nso unlike the concept set list there was nothing to click. Give it\nsortable headers over id, name, author, created and updated, opening on\nmost recently updated to match the concept set list.\n\nThe four analysis lists had the opposite problem: their headers looked\nsortable but the sort state was passed down one way, so clicks were\nemitted and discarded and every list stayed pinned to last modified.\nSeed the table from the prop and let it own the order after that.\n\nAlso relabel the cohort list''s modified column to Updated, which is what\n2.x called it and what the concept set list already uses.","tree":{"sha":"e1c0654c1eeb951b1ebbe7360322bcd25b6ddce5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OHDSI/Atlas3/git/trees/e1c0654c1eeb951b1ebbe7360322bcd25b6ddce5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OHDSI/Atlas3/git/commits/ce85402467a4b972e25e4e84f377e864c3ea31c6","verification":{"payload":"tree e1c0654c1eeb951b1ebbe7360322bcd25b6ddce5\nparent 1814e5faa47c9d29158670ff16e254095b9b1fe3\nauthor Peter Hoffmann <954078+p-hoffmann@users.noreply.github.com> 1787335957 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787335957 -0400\n\nLet the cohort and analysis lists be sorted by column (#280)\n\nThe cohort list was a hand written table whose headers were plain text,\nso unlike the concept set list there was nothing to click. Give it\nsortable headers over id, name, author, created and updated, opening on\nmost recently updated to match the concept set list.\n\nThe four analysis lists had the opposite problem: their headers looked\nsortable but the sort state was passed down one way, so clicks were\nemitted and discarded and every list stayed pinned to last modified.\nSeed the table from the prop and let it own the order after that.\n\nAlso relabel the cohort list''s modified column to Updated, which is what\n2.x called it and what the concept set list already uses.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqiJUVCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAVWgQAJaEZ1YFL3sTBhWlHJGiOOcl\nohZ9/f3E/nnSviUv/nwX61rTKPDfIkxViuz3ucaEk+7xbrELnWe2enyu00oDHuks\ndr83nmQaEPz7lXjN7+xLmIoFes8VWSH7Zz55AWH3P9pZ2Jl6qNo+LNmh/gRmx+E2\nwNMqXDZRgM/HSm1pae08PbZj7FJbh4S7+rN5zzmvc2jJoaJZUboiWAv9J5TdXD4e\nqWx+uz2LIRTVcpMDXq4snaSShk6BGF/UEKDrCqKHT0VYco7Oct2XGXK+PM/F9xXo\nLBps8pJedEt+3yJR+S3k18PW1pl/SDEjciJHGrk2vT3Lt+mJ7n/i0KjGpWOhsIO+\nvGWTfhD3iKagzDDH7BvCEyTHUyoQCWzRQ0888BHPFKwwNrgLOMBgLAvGlUSgSkkV\nLEGxl7A6bCjpx1hAvTGDDRf17G1GUaCY/cCnsLlbXL+k+7wXY6e5kPTASftpgq9y\nNm+8/OsNfMj3WX/9v65LKDDM54anqP2r1HLgAe9OgQjXGQl6CV7yeagK0lOpljrl\nL0F7wLA/nEHLkRLkqmYS7SUHMp+j1T+a5psNOvBm4ldfDt3X1TgYIxW8JAGF79WX\n/vce6i29Tl74+tf6BnBXqTWNmntm53keHOhylfP2natzN7+6Tw7x5xDKgL8D6InN\nHMHGrWjYqDS6Jnpo8iP9\n=hqM/\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-21T18:12:38Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow