url":"https://api.github.com/users/p-hoffmann/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/p-hoffmann","id":954078,"login":"p-hoffmann","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk1NDA3OA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/p-hoffmann/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/p-hoffmann/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/p-hoffmann/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/p-hoffmann/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/p-hoffmann/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/p-hoffmann","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OHDSI/Atlas3/commits/c1b7bcffe939f5822c849d0fb58f64bd824e5619/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-19T23:02:47Z","email":"954078+p-hoffmann@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Peter Hoffmann"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-19T23:02:47Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Handle OIDC one-time-code redemption on /oauth/callback (#256) (#259)\n\nThe OAuth/SAML/OpenID callback guard only looked for a token already\nsitting in localStorage or a cookie. Google/OIDC providers instead\nredirect back with ?code={otc}, which nothing consumed, so the guard\nfell straight through to \"no token received\" and the login failed.\n\nAdd AuthService.redeemOTC(code) to exchange the code for a JWT via\nWebAPI''s /user/login/otc, and have the callback guard use it whenever\na code is present, before falling back to the existing handoff paths.","tree":{"sha":"54d62904459b3a9d35a4e2eca3360a18fd7444cd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OHDSI/Atlas3/git/trees/54d62904459b3a9d35a4e2eca3360a18fd7444cd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OHDSI/Atlas3/git/commits/c1b7bcffe939f5822c849d0fb58f64bd824e5619","verification":{"payload":"tree 54d62904459b3a9d35a4e2eca3360a18fd7444cd\nparent 179f2072274056cfaec15fb1934a255bcf3f8a58\nauthor Peter Hoffmann <954078+p-hoffmann@users.noreply.github.com> 1787180567 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787180567 -0400\n\nHandle OIDC one-time-code redemption on /oauth/callback (#256) (#259)\n\nThe OAuth/SAML/OpenID callback guard only looked for a token already\nsitting in localStorage or a cookie. Google/OIDC providers instead\nredirect back with ?code={otc}, which nothing consumed, so the guard\nfell straight through to \"no token received\" and the login failed.\n\nAdd AuthService.redeemOTC(code) to exchange the code for a JWT via\nWebAPI''s /user/login/otc, and have the callback guard use it whenever\na code is present, before falling back to the existing handoff paths.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqhjYXCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAOGcQACYvAFGf83XgiOn4BXWVRzFC\nWQZIlcddPhMcNDgwRVXu4o7AZ2G90IVR1+FzUjZYHOa8AwhdGjf1BlWuR05FqoNx\ncAG1rPKfKTCFgbqePMUvawcnUH1IVEbPbw5RmGa326wtFe0XF4vLQAEggEZr23g4\n7/Uvj7fC2cmFycplz0nOJzpLrI183nnj4cKZNLz9g+ZPAGX7ZbOO227+Dnkpp3yJ\nnu3Lf7b/Ko1P4JppNVuBfknXrIK3vi4qBkjK12p8ayxIlYMPUrBjOiyyBX+7ogbT\nfcn1vDGfJ/WfdmB9GlWdGu7KSXn5rl35bOO4CxHxK0RfftiQtr0jAHNEGsuvTjHr\nenKyLM0anhy+1ILQpSYJZ3nOprcCrcWlm1P34XxQ60K2LaYO0Ufpx86JtTP8bjnd\nN3isdj8/FUEUsBgzvzCb/q1VmjahSK0QU7s6BQ8M0mGI2u9/ZgZ7fMERG6gva2dI\n4Nqn/QrW5OM+kNcWh3o/7nRJF2Ek0xqgnR/sBRcOqmSAXi9Yw4ppBJFeEEXPqk81\nbk37a/jlgKveD4n37lRNoqfeABjhqx2wcMJHerU1+cuUVcqP0EilmbtnUCHMf+zf\ncTnnDgf8/UPlApL0jer4RpZxiHOxYsc9S+Slvx5tQKOEpFqRs2wB5MCyOG5WmJu7\njRoTGN99AhEQNCSS2i5p\n=ZZHg\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-19T23:02:48Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/OHDSI/Atlas3/commit/c1b7bcffe939f5822c849d0fb58f64bd824e5619","node_id":"C_kwDOQWYjcNoAKGMxYjdiY2ZmZTkzOWY1ODIyYzg0OWQwZmI1OGY2NGJkODI0ZTU2MTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/OHDSI/Atlas3/commit/179f2072274056cfaec15fb1934a255bcf3f8a58","sha":"179f2072274056cfaec15fb1934a255bcf3f8a58","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OHDSI/Atlas3/commits/179f2072274056cfaec15fb1934a255bcf3f8a58"}],"sha":"c1b7bcffe939f5822c849d0fb58f64bd824e5619","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OHDSI/Atlas3/commits/c1b7bcffe939f5822c849d0fb58f64bd824e5619"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6818777?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrisknoll/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrisknoll/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrisknoll/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrisknoll/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/chrisknoll","id":6818777,"login":"chrisknoll","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY4MTg3Nzc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrisknoll/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrisknoll/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrisknoll/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrisknoll/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrisknoll/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrisknoll","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OHDSI/Atlas3/commits/179f2072274056cfaec15fb1934a255bcf3f8a58/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-19T19:33:38Z","email":"cknoll@ohdsi.org","name":"Chris Knoll"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-19T19:33:38Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Introduced native circe-types cohort editor. (#165)\n\nThis PR completes the migration and stabilization of the new CIRCE-based cohort editor, with a focus on correctness, maintainability, and feature parity with ATLAS 2.x.\n\nHighlights\n- Migrated the cohort editor to the native CIRCE object model, removing the legacy Atlas conversion layer and aligning the editor directly with the WebAPI payload.\n- Improved type safety and schema validation by synchronizing the TypeScript/Zod model with the Java object model and strengthening compile-time validation.\n- Refactored the editor architecture to use a single shared document with late-binding accessors, eliminating stale references, duplicate state, and render-time mutations.\n- Fixed numerous loading, saving, validation, navigation, and generation issues, including race conditions, dirty tracking, version preview behavior, and restoring ATLAS 2.15 generation semantics.\n- Completed and hardened the Pythia/agent integration, ensuring proposals are translated correctly into CIRCE structures and failures are reported accurately.\n- Significantly expanded the test suite, restoring migration coverage, adding schema and performance tests, fixing flaky unit tests, and repairing Playwright/e2e coverage.\n\nThis PR also includes numerous bug fixes, refactorings, and cleanup work identified during the CIRCE migration and subsequent merge with develop.","tree":{"sha":"32ccaab2bfa1e6ef32aaed0e72e438d9625677ea","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OHDSI/Atlas3/git/trees/32ccaab2bfa1e6ef32aaed0e72e438d9625677ea"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OHDSI/Atlas3/git/commits/179f2072274056cfaec15fb1934a255bcf3f8a58","verification":{"payload":"tree 32ccaab2bfa1e6ef32aaed0e72e438d9625677ea\nparent 4c0623d84fff16295df9e40833fc8dbeda4268ce\nauthor Chris Knoll <cknoll@ohdsi.org> 1787168018 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787168018 -0400\n\nIntroduced native circe-types cohort editor. (#165)\n\nThis PR completes the migration and stabilization of the new CIRCE-based cohort editor, with a focus on correctness, maintainability, and feature parity with ATLAS 2.x.\n\nHighlights\n- Migrated the cohort editor to the native CIRCE object model, removing the legacy Atlas conversion layer and aligning the editor directly with the WebAPI payload.\n- Improved type safety and schema validation by synchronizing the TypeScript/Zod model with the Java object model and strengthening compile-time validation.\n- Refactored the editor architecture to use a single shared document with late-binding accessors, eliminating stale references, duplicate state, and render-time mutations.\n- Fixed numerous loading, saving, validation, navigation, and generation issues, including race conditions, dirty tracking, version preview behavior, and restoring ATLAS 2.15 generation semantics.\n- Completed and hardened the Pythia/agent integration, ensuring proposals are translated correctly into CIRCE structures and failures are reported accurately.\n- Significantly expanded the test suite, restoring migration coverage, adding schema and performance tests, fixing flaky unit tests, and repairing Playwright/e2e coverage.\n\nThis PR also includes numerous bug fixes, refactorings, and cleanup work identified during the CIRCE migration and subsequent merge with develop.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqhgUSCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAHhwQAFHFLT/3G1fbyYH7TKcL8qJ0\nscqV4o2yiTnv0bPyS7ai4v2cX+2YtWu28hnXStH1mPWgJMQbKisp0WkviSn9Hl40\nD2es40vkWXmy5ES+0v6hOAb2Y+nEYll1zJZZHkOMktQzXNsMc6WiXuTUrWe7eGHQ\nB75