ttps://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/OHDSI/Atlas3/commit/9baa99a647d8214dbc3fe911e9c7f93fb28dba00","node_id":"C_kwDOQWYjcNoAKDliYWE5OWE2NDdkODIxNGRiYzNmZTkxMWU5YzdmOTNmYjI4ZGJhMDA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/OHDSI/Atlas3/commit/459d1990d7118d8759f7e9bd4ec5fe872194698b","sha":"459d1990d7118d8759f7e9bd4ec5fe872194698b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OHDSI/Atlas3/commits/459d1990d7118d8759f7e9bd4ec5fe872194698b"}],"sha":"9baa99a647d8214dbc3fe911e9c7f93fb28dba00","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OHDSI/Atlas3/commits/9baa99a647d8214dbc3fe911e9c7f93fb28dba00"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/954078?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/p-hoffmann/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/p-hoffmann/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/p-hoffmann/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/p-hoffmann/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/p-hoffmann","id":954078,"login":"p-hoffmann","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk1NDA3OA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/p-hoffmann/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/p-hoffmann/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/p-hoffmann/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/p-hoffmann/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/p-hoffmann/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/p-hoffmann","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OHDSI/Atlas3/commits/459d1990d7118d8759f7e9bd4ec5fe872194698b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-14T14:52:01Z","email":"954078+p-hoffmann@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Peter Hoffmann"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-14T14:52:01Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(characterization): filter the feature-analysis picker by facet (#251)\n\nPicking an analysis to add offered a name search over a list that runs to\nabout 1,400 entries in a real deployment, which is not enough to find\nanything (#216).\n\nThe dialog now carries the same facets Atlas 2.15 puts on its own\n\"Choose a Feature analyses...\" picker: Type, Domain, Created, Updated,\nAuthor and Designs, each option counted against the rows currently shown\n(\"Criteria set (1154)\"). 2.15 does not facet on stat type, so neither\ndoes this.\n\nCreated and Updated use 2.15''s three buckets — This Week, Last Week,\n2+ Weeks Ago — computed against a reference time captured when the dialog\nopens, so a row cannot drift between buckets while it is open. Designs\nsplits the signed-in user''s own analyses from the rest; the login is\npassed in as a prop rather than read from the store inside the picker, so\nit stays presentational and its consumers do not need a Pinia instance to\nrender a list.\n\nThe filter bar itself is the one the concept list already uses, lifted\nout of ConceptFacetFilters into AtlasFacetFilterBar so that a third list\nneeding this does not write a third version of it. ConceptFacetFilters\nremains as the concept-flavoured wrapper that supplies the concept facets\nand the column i18n keys, so concept search is unchanged; its spec moves\nto the new class names because the markup now lives in the shared\ncomponent.\n\nThe facet machinery is useConceptFacets, which was already generic over\nthe item type and needed no change: it takes the definitions and a\nsearch-text extractor and returns the cross-facet counts.\n\nText search still works as before, and is now driven through the shared\nbar rather than a local ref.","tree":{"sha":"248e2b60235220868d5ead2046a4e3bbbbd092f5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OHDSI/Atlas3/git/trees/248e2b60235220868d5ead2046a4e3bbbbd092f5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OHDSI/Atlas3/git/commits/459d1990d7118d8759f7e9bd4ec5fe872194698b","verification":{"payload":"tree 248e2b60235220868d5ead2046a4e3bbbbd092f5\nparent 086edb9dfeb998c422d456171bfd180b3035bed2\nauthor Peter Hoffmann <954078+p-hoffmann@users.noreply.github.com> 1786719121 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786719121 +0800\n\nfeat(characterization): filter the feature-analysis picker by facet (#251)\n\nPicking an analysis to add offered a name search over a list that runs to\nabout 1,400 entries in a real deployment, which is not enough to find\nanything (#216).\n\nThe dialog now carries the same facets Atlas 2.15 puts on its own\n\"Choose a Feature analyses...\" picker: Type, Domain, Created, Updated,\nAuthor and Designs, each option counted against the rows currently shown\n(\"Criteria set (1154)\"). 2.15 does not facet on stat type, so neither\ndoes this.\n\nCreated and Updated use 2.15''s three buckets — This Week, Last Week,\n2+ Weeks Ago — computed against a reference time captured when the dialog\nopens, so a row cannot drift between buckets while it is open. Designs\nsplits the signed-in user''s own analyses from the rest; the login is\npassed in as a prop rather than read from the store inside the picker, so\nit stays presentational and its consumers do not need a Pinia instance to\nrender a list.\n\nThe filter bar itself is the one the concept list already uses, lifted\nout of ConceptFacetFilters into AtlasFacetFilterBar so that a third list\nneeding this does not write a third version of it. ConceptFacetFilters\nremains as the concept-flavoured wrapper that supplies the concept facets\nand the column i18n keys, so concept search is unchanged; its spec moves\nto the new class names because the markup now lives in the shared\ncomponent.\n\nThe facet machinery is useConceptFacets, which was already generic over\nthe item type and needed no change: it takes the definitions and a\nsearch-text extractor and returns the cross-facet counts.\n\nText search still works as before, and is now driven through the shared\nbar rather than a local ref.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqfyuRCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAATA0QAIopJvNO0+brORC+hLTmwByz\nOxRys+aAsycXMhVLGCyhER6+ocCZN/qHg6DKKJbv5IPaqwPgTF0qq3GDqM6gvPRB\nbS4qNE0o2/uJucF5ZP7/WL3W7sVeeU0uPDQHv2oH+GP5kcdTF1I6QPcrklStZD1L\nlwsmoo44K9c597CBju7HRFY6162I6R5HzwkvqcjSya+7LPLtOAl92sGcjn1wFQ/P\nxpXZbsA+CbOogEHy7BkWj4c75kcsdthTnAcAdjotZZJ1NGfBQyAy7i20nWMFJZ9K\neOrn96gJJXtgXipZ4bM0//EQVeIZ1CWjLwM4fDLPbYw2wlv82SZxtSsllYOfb7Lh\nYz37VMuuznJirSwGR0Am+McjOWNczOKSEOXx3MrEbbT9VSb23i2aj9GXOpP4K7dR\nqTIKrRue/TyiSmlTnMwHhx6+Ta6qVD2IyURnsgFPyEXs8jl6Ja7fihAEXHSD3oPl\niC9GRZfomYJ8W+Z3rtc+GCptQyjMg5unFd1q7+DaEEatm6cseDt8HPQsT83dQddG\nGp/UC8gbH5y/gEfWI8aOE2JYgR3YWcMpvlKNuU0DL1wGmZbeCYkyUIo5rGYGcyML\naLb+t7fjWCUInLv6rlYb3WhxYWFMJyBACyqNpXmVdP9quRcHysgJexSQfB6oS7hB\nxgvUMQP8DG92euw2zAe0\n=oMaW\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-14T14:52:29Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/OHDSI/Atlas3/commit/459d1990d7118d8759f7e9bd4ec5fe872194698b","node_id":"C_kwDOQWYjcNoAKDQ1OWQxOTkwZDcxMThkODc1OWY3ZTliZDRlYzVmZTg3MjE5NDY5OGI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/OHDSI/Atlas3/commit/086edb9dfeb998c422d456171bfd180b3035bed2","sha":"086edb9dfeb998c422d456171bfd180b3035bed2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OHDSI/Atlas3/commits/086edb9dfeb998c422d456171bfd180b3035bed2"}],"sha":"459d1990d7118d8759f7e9bd4ec5fe872194698b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OHDSI/Atlas3/commits/459d1990d7118d8759f7e9bd4ec5fe872194698b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/954078?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/p-hoffmann/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/p-hoffmann/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/p-hoffmann/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/p-hoffmann/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/p-hoffmann","id":954078,"login":"p-hoffmann","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk1NDA3OA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/p-hoffmann/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/p-hoffmann/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/p-hoffmann/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/p-hoffmann/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/p-hoffmann/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/p-hoffmann","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OHDSI/Atlas3/commits/086edb9dfeb998c422d456171bfd180b3035bed2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-14T10:03:04Z","email":"954078+p-hoffmann@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Peter Hoffmann"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-14T10:03:04Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Show progress while the concept hierarchy switches between tree and flat (#249)\n\nOn a concept with a large subtree, switching the hierarchy viewer between\nTree and Flat takes a couple of seconds with no sign anything is\nhappening, so the button gets clicked again.\n\nRebuilding the row list is synchronous, which is why simply setting a\nflag alongside the view change does not help: Vue batches both into one\nupdate and the expensive render blocks the frame, so the spinner never\nreaches the screen. Set the flag, hand control back to the event loop so\nit can paint, and only then swap the view.\n\nWhile the switch is in flight the rows are held back and a loading row\ntakes their place, and both view buttons are disabled so the extra\nclicks the delay used to invite cannot queue up behind it.\n\nExisting toolbar tests drove the toggle and asserted on the new rows\nafter a single tick, which no longer covers the deferred swap, so they\ngo through a helper that flushes it.\n\nThis makes the wait legible rather than shorter. Rendering thousands of\nrows at once is the underlying cost, and virtualising the table would be\nthe way to remove it.\n\nFixes #207","tree":{"sha":"e32cdd6fb80b96d560f3f11e45b235d9e3e7e39b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OHDSI/Atlas3/git/trees/e32cdd6fb80b96d560f3f11e45b235d9e3e7e39b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OHDSI/Atlas3/git/commits/086edb9dfeb998c422d456171bfd180b3035bed2","verification":{"payload":"tree e32cdd6fb80b96d560f3f11e45b235d9e3e7e39b\nparent c7b188d7f3eaef433a6c002aea9d1460eb1a38fc\nauthor Peter Hoffmann <954078+p-hoffmann@users.noreply.github.com> 1786701784 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786701784 +0800\n\nShow progress while the concept hierarchy switches between tree and flat (#249)\n\nOn a concept with a large subtree, switching the hierarchy viewer between\nTree and Flat takes a couple of seconds with no sign anything is\nhappening, so the button gets clicked again.\n\nRebuilding the row list is synchronous, which is why simply setting a\nflag alongside the view change does not help: Vue batches both into one\nupdate and the expensive render blocks the frame, so the spinner never\nreaches the screen. Set the flag, hand control back to the event loop so\nit can paint, and only then swap the view.\n\nWhile the switch is in flight the rows are held back and a loading row\ntakes their place, and both view buttons are disabled so the extra\nclicks the delay used to invite cannot queue up behind it.\n\nExisting toolbar tests drove the toggle and asserted on the new rows\nafter a single tick, which no longer covers the deferred swap, so they\ngo through a helper that flushes it.\n\nThis makes the wait legible rather than shorter. Rendering thousands of\nrows at once is the underlying cost, and virtualising the table would be\nthe way to remove it.\n\nFixes #207","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqfufYCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAATVkQAIhyvYtauEfRw08TGpgkLb3s\nWYs4gntCJ8v++y90wHJwCi1j3GvNLpc2IFwRYPrlmxV2FFb7pHVz5vRwxlxnhkyA\nEZhxM6ujuZNMWPJajz9CZ0BX0c8mshu80trI/LnJODCW7ZoxBYq9rmdtiwjdTw+H\nDAcaRdTT8oFjWJpPMXGh4E46Hs7SRUyUuTprXWDddzrlFj6nr8iigdYH1O078eM1\n5aJfiHip/0Yv3px+Lydaufgj3eaj7UZ7IQqzZL38bDzAATJ9pe2ca+hZrPU7xjyk\n/dhiwr0LxgOysLwQfFm3KH1WH8E3h7//89DBfM/+tyaVgi+5ivttq82u2MvsayV2\nCudhOWsAJGiDP+sVpz4Jzq1rgai4bE93jSrU1RrpEQrUDWpUMLMDN/Hcody6Nui1\naZ9Z+BhDHSRKnaB8aaOTL3JLJ3gVuuXtHdGg+eirXQds5mO65lD9mUY+z70snnt/\ndvPIQAof8aG8YkdT1jHEmm7VIGHOfpYQSkFZnuzoo8TlcBMSVGuGxmi8wHQipkgR\ngT4LYbya7nNQx6WAdHJdyTlZTpPsbI1FbWRm5i5FGEZbgjzWXosHSv6055BStr2H\nAfrkQWvTxz50E8Pw1TFdK3HXVSlrIWPWGJi4BZYctYzPcVbBmfehDeiio2txSCa1\norJB3BHKzyD60rvjYA4w\n=PZpT\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-14T10:03:08Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/OHDSI/Atlas3/commit/086edb9dfeb998c422d456171bfd180b3035bed2","node_id":"C_kwDOQWYjcNoAKDA4NmVkYjlkZmViOTk4YzQyMmQ0NTYxNzFiZmQxODBiMzAzNWJlZDI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/OHDSI/Atlas3/commit/c7b188d7f3eaef433a6c002aea9d1460eb1a38fc","sha":"c7b188d7f3eaef433a6c002aea9d1460eb1a38fc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OHDSI/Atlas3/commits/c7b188d7f3eaef433a6c002aea9d1460eb1a38fc"}],"sha":"086edb9dfeb998c422d456171bfd180b3035bed2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OHDSI/Atlas3/commits/086edb9dfeb998c422d456171bfd180b3035bed2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/954078?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/p-hoffmann/events{/