ha":"6b051c7c4826f6895668acef88ec25f7aa0c4dc3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OHDSI/Atlas3/commits/6b051c7c4826f6895668acef88ec25f7aa0c4dc3"}],"sha":"c7b188d7f3eaef433a6c002aea9d1460eb1a38fc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OHDSI/Atlas3/commits/c7b188d7f3eaef433a6c002aea9d1460eb1a38fc"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/954078?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/p-hoffmann/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/p-hoffmann/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/p-hoffmann/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/p-hoffmann/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/p-hoffmann","id":954078,"login":"p-hoffmann","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk1NDA3OA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/p-hoffmann/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/p-hoffmann/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/p-hoffmann/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/p-hoffmann/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/p-hoffmann/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/p-hoffmann","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OHDSI/Atlas3/commits/6b051c7c4826f6895668acef88ec25f7aa0c4dc3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-14T09:27:43Z","email":"954078+p-hoffmann@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Peter Hoffmann"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-14T09:27:43Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Fix attribute concept set picker reverting to unselected for id 0 (#238)\n\n* Fix attribute concept set picker reverting to unselected for id 0 (#213)\n\nThe concept set attribute editor checked !attribute.conceptSet.id to\ndecide whether to show the picker button or the selected-set chip. id\n0 is a valid, real concept set id (the first set in an imported\ncohort), and the truthy check misfired on it, showing the ''Select\nConcept Set'' picker instead of the chip even though a concept set was\nselected. Other components in the same area already guard this\ncorrectly with an explicit id == null check.\n\nUse the same explicit null check here.\n\n* Treat the empty-string placeholder as unselected, not as a chosen set\n\nThe first version of this fix swapped a truthy test on the concept set id\nfor `id == null`. That fixed id 0 but broke the other placeholder: adding\na concept set attribute seeds `{ id: '''', name: '''' }`, and an empty string\nis not null, so the attribute rendered an empty chip instead of the\n\"Select Concept Set\" button. CriteriaEventCard seeds the same shape.\n\nUse hasNumericConceptSetId, which already encodes exactly this rule: a\nfinite non-negative number counts as chosen, so 0 qualifies, while null,\nundefined and '''' do not. The helper now accepts a missing reference so\ncallers do not have to test for it twice, though the templates keep an\nexplicit guard so the v-else branch stays narrowed.\n\nDrugExposureStrategy and EventConceptSetField carried the same `== null`\ntest against the same placeholder, so they move to the helper too.\n\nThe regression showed up as a coverage drop: with `''''` no longer routed\nto the picker, the picker branch lost the only test that reached it.","tree":{"sha":"a344698ee16b84f3fcd42ac319a338f5962ba701","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OHDSI/Atlas3/git/trees/a344698ee16b84f3fcd42ac319a338f5962ba701"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OHDSI/Atlas3/git/commits/6b051c7c4826f6895668acef88ec25f7aa0c4dc3","verification":{"payload":"tree a344698ee16b84f3fcd42ac319a338f5962ba701\nparent 1f1a7cd69e1f1ff14cf12bbb2849a055adf78a74\nauthor Peter Hoffmann <954078+p-hoffmann@users.noreply.github.com> 1786699663 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786699663 +0800\n\nFix attribute concept set picker reverting to unselected for id 0 (#238)\n\n* Fix attribute concept set picker reverting to unselected for id 0 (#213)\n\nThe concept set attribute editor checked !attribute.conceptSet.id to\ndecide whether to show the picker button or the selected-set chip. id\n0 is a valid, real concept set id (the first set in an imported\ncohort), and the truthy check misfired on it, showing the ''Select\nConcept Set'' picker instead of the chip even though a concept set was\nselected. Other components in the same area already guard this\ncorrectly with an explicit id == null check.\n\nUse the same explicit null check here.\n\n* Treat the empty-string placeholder as unselected, not as a chosen set\n\nThe first version of this fix swapped a truthy test on the concept set id\nfor `id == null`. That fixed id 0 but broke the other placeholder: adding\na concept set attribute seeds `{ id: '''', name: '''' }`, and an empty string\nis not null, so the attribute rendered an empty chip instead of the\n\"Select Concept Set\" button. CriteriaEventCard seeds the same shape.\n\nUse hasNumericConceptSetId, which already encodes exactly this rule: a\nfinite non-negative number counts as chosen, so 0 qualifies, while null,\nundefined and '''' do not. The helper now accepts a missing reference so\ncallers do not have to test for it twice, though the templates keep an\nexplicit guard so the v-else branch stays narrowed.\n\nDrugExposureStrategy and EventConceptSetField carried the same `== null`\ntest against the same placeholder, so they move to the helper too.\n\nThe regression showed up as a coverage drop: with `''''` no longer routed\nto the picker, the picker branch lost the only test that reached it.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqft+PCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAANDEQAJulhKBCdQ0AEm8CubDJjsOg\nFnijQM+5GLwGk8MFBZv1nXI7pL97uN/ZUjYae/jmNp4+2PPGSmaPwvJyWuZAcu6G\nyRV0JpKcc4SeFrjgJzfzPArDtURfVft24x4NogjhmX/c9cIM910jm9gFCqAbCws8\nCTNChrh0S+IkRp7fZCb6Ey/kmvpSt/ekEB9FgycA4/eymce4SjZIk1GvOUJqYP7K\n59GiElEnJtQLR8/8f0c1ghAhLzc51ja3+lEadE77ON/xiwE