n","id":954078,"login":"p-hoffmann","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk1NDA3OA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/p-hoffmann/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/p-hoffmann/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/p-hoffmann/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/p-hoffmann/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/p-hoffmann/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/p-hoffmann","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OHDSI/Atlas3/commits/35668b71f69f14c4c30780ab938df6b8fea19fae/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-14T07:05:41Z","email":"954078+p-hoffmann@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Peter Hoffmann"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-14T07:05:41Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Show the resulting concept set after adding a concept, not the search view (#236)\n\n* Show the resulting concept set after adding a concept, not the search view (#210)\n\nA new concept set opens on the Search tab so users can start adding\nconcepts right away, but adding one left the search UI showing with no\nvisible confirmation that anything had happened, since the added\nconcept only appears on the Selected tab. Switch to Selected right\nafter the first concept lands in a previously-empty set, on both the\nsingle-add and recommend-add paths, but not on later adds, so the\nsearch-then-add-several workflow the Search default was built for\nstill works.\n\n* Cover the recommend-add path of the Selected-tab switch","tree":{"sha":"660f6aa7a85298092b3633506510cf7d4d56e27a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OHDSI/Atlas3/git/trees/660f6aa7a85298092b3633506510cf7d4d56e27a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OHDSI/Atlas3/git/commits/35668b71f69f14c4c30780ab938df6b8fea19fae","verification":{"payload":"tree 660f6aa7a85298092b3633506510cf7d4d56e27a\nparent 78885d296c4c1ac8cb34a8a70788cbfdc18e720a\nauthor Peter Hoffmann <954078+p-hoffmann@users.noreply.github.com> 1786691141 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786691141 +0800\n\nShow the resulting concept set after adding a concept, not the search view (#236)\n\n* Show the resulting concept set after adding a concept, not the search view (#210)\n\nA new concept set opens on the Search tab so users can start adding\nconcepts right away, but adding one left the search UI showing with no\nvisible confirmation that anything had happened, since the added\nconcept only appears on the Selected tab. Switch to Selected right\nafter the first concept lands in a previously-empty set, on both the\nsingle-add and recommend-add paths, but not on later adds, so the\nsearch-then-add-several workflow the Search default was built for\nstill works.\n\n* Cover the recommend-add path of the Selected-tab switch","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqfr5FCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAbcoQAJ3WBWLyR6MJkJE6TNOjFONe\nE8KGPZODR4xx9FYnQI4N2QoAtBOOiz6D23cpahYbSVZVheThQdrhF4Q/cBa0H+wd\nt0qlyGoSB3JlZgjdR8E2EmWqXdFTyD19RR4gZCdEQGGQkQQaqF/4QTbgmIpsr3dN\na9FXN/UejPzGiocAa67/7bd2SFaA0m+0svMdLrm3MORfIn7C4TVYqO7MHb+NHdM9\ngk0bAfnU/ltDC6zkArKVkDjjAkQLVi31AYSUqPiGqHN1mgHGH5maESoYF4HuFUjv\nMLiGzPS0f022DCIIbD/kDA26FBg4gDJCl7eC4HWDdRP7aZaRaEAerDCnY3+ErX8U\nRdug3oqyPbABuA58btFYFQv5yDNM0f/9hWmSRVH9PRVUD+E/o0FLllVnLbeQung3\nts4vb5dOgHsHr84b/pN3UyNeUPHgY/rJTvoFsyOw7urQdxGzaW2NM/8fV6mW/X5L\nzf19jptT6F+89+rwOeqcCtKpjTw+XkRXDafQ5OQ61f03WJNzYL++JNeTDm7cET/Y\nqEVuJcdn+QyJKYTuDzPUnPcDeY4TWjg8atWqZFDQ3PIaqAoFcME0xMGX3Gq16jDU\n8Z0ClHlv9qDHadlvzHmg+cWAeGn08pdxpoG6rIOr10YC4EBddyqJxHbFSLb+kvgZ\nrc9ZylVdz08o0whlMe/Y\n=Flg1\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-14T07:05:44Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/OHDSI/Atlas3/commit/35668b71f69f14c4c30780ab938df6b8fea19fae","node_id":"C_kwDOQWYjcNoAKDM1NjY4YjcxZjY5ZjE0YzRjMzA3ODBhYjkzOGRmNmI4ZmVhMTlmYWU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/OHDSI/Atlas3/commit/78885d296c4c1ac8cb34a8a70788cbfdc18e720a","sha":"78885d296c4c1ac8cb34a8a70788cbfdc18e720a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OHDSI/Atlas3/commits/78885d296c4c1ac8cb34a8a70788cbfdc18e720a"}],"sha":"35668b71f69f14c4c30780ab938df6b8fea19fae","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OHDSI/Atlas3/commits/35668b71f69f14c4c30780ab938df6b8fea19fae"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/954078?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/p-hoffmann/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/p-hoffmann/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/p-hoffmann/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/p-hoffmann/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/p-hoffmann","id":954078,"login":"p-hoffmann","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk1NDA3OA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/p-hoffmann/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/p-hoffmann/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/p-hoffmann/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/p-hoffmann/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/p-hoffmann/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/p-hoffmann","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OHDSI/Atlas3/commits/78885d296c4c1ac8cb34a8a70788cbfdc18e720a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-14T06:26:03Z","email":"954078+p-hoffmann@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Peter Hoffmann"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-14T06:26:03Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Show Close instead of Cancel when a cohort has no unsaved changes (#240)\n\n* Show Close instead of Cancel when a cohort has no unsaved changes (#220)\n\nThe header button always read Cancel, even when nothing had been\nedited, which reads as more alarming than necessary. The discard\nconfirmation already only fires when hasUnsavedChanges is true (the\nroute-leave guard checks it directly), so this is purely a label\nchange: show Close when isDirty is false and keep Cancel, with its\nexisting confirmation behavior, when it is true.\n\n* Retarget the cohort close e2e tests at the button, not its label\n\nThe two breadcrumb tests looked the toolbar button up by accessible\nname, so renaming it to Close for an unedited cohort broke them. Naming\nit Close instead is not enough on its own: the navbar carries its own\nClose control, so a name lookup matches two buttons and trips Playwright''s\nstrict mode.\n\nGive the toolbar button a test id, as its neighbouring export button\nalready has, and select on that. The tests still assert the label reads\nClose, which is the behaviour this branch introduces, but no longer\ndepend on it being unique in the page.","tree":{"sha":"662389a46812c60dcb05f14501b748aa47fccbb0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OHDSI/Atlas3/git/trees/662389a46812c60dcb05f14501b748aa47fccbb0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OHDSI/Atlas3/git/commits/78885d296c4c1ac8cb34a8a70788cbfdc18e720a","verification":{"payload":"tree 662389a46812c60dcb05f14501b748aa47fccbb0\nparent bfa29f10d9c88145a30554b0454553c4b74907dc\nauthor Peter Hoffmann <954078+p-hoffmann@users.noreply.github.com> 1786688763 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786688763 +0800\n\nShow Close instead of Cancel when a cohort has no unsaved changes (#240)\n\n* Show Close instead of Cancel when a cohort has no unsaved changes (#220)\n\nThe header button always read Cancel, even when nothing had been\nedited, which reads as more alarming than necessary. The discard\nconfirmation already only fires when hasUnsavedChanges is true (the\nroute-leave guard checks it directly), so this is purely a label\nchange: show Close when isDirty is false and keep Cancel, with its\nexisting confirmation behavior, when it is true.\n\n* Retarget the cohort close e2e tests at the button, not its label\n\nThe two breadcrumb tests looked the toolbar button up by accessible\nname, so renaming it to Close for an unedited cohort broke them. Naming\nit Close instead is not enough on its own: the navbar carries its own\nClose control, so a name lookup matches two buttons and trips Playwright''s\nstrict mode.\n\nGive the toolbar button a test id, as its neighbouring export button\nalready has, and select on that. The tests still assert the label reads\nClose, which is the behaviour this branch introduces, but no longer\ndepend on it being unique in the page.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqfrT7CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAhhgQAHQxluWgqs/Z3KDQa2hnaTf1\nrkBlOK8vAcKEcTbigbp54qjvtTfhXZilA7mBRvYnOqYzNbRqi9lt1R1c2xeey2zt\n9RXAXHjA1BK0Gr/Wk67KNdq1xEy4yEdhAGu+AUqvXSvjo+/UbqRr38jtg/U7nt79\nfYXrBVvW2dacPVC/famCqu3zvxWWNb6QqMaDUBJEn4HoI6BizOB1wFyqbynpQv+6\ndzViGwB7bPvPQoAKCQDSR02FKZ0tFsS6SxzxbIAIldEM7gAKOCOkXMRDI/ru/FlB\nf7O1scMy98Isbta1kozsrzU3EAP3KeEvehdW0ZGTUsXDiAubQSFboFlZwTqjmTaG\nS6g/tZbl539gKBU9zQWbDCIBjzLSrc9Ohepi6