com","name":"Peter Hoffmann"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-14T06:20:13Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Make the active tab clearly distinguishable in shared page tabs (#235)\n\n* Make the active tab clearly distinguishable in shared page tabs (#209)\n\nThe Search/Recommend tab selector (and every other page using the\nshared .page-tabs style) relied only on a 2px slider and a color shift\nto show which tab was active, easy to miss at a glance. Bump the\nselected tab''s weight and slider thickness.\n\n* Re-record the visual baselines the tab styling changes\n\nBumping the selected tab''s weight and slider thickness changes how every\npage carrying .page-tabs renders, so the committed screenshots for\ncharacterizations, concept sets, incidence rates and pathways no longer\nmatch.\n\nRe-recorded in mcr.microsoft.com/playwright:v1.61.1-noble, the same image\nthe e2e workflow runs, so the baselines match CI''s font rendering rather\nthan a host machine''s. Only the five tabbed pages changed; the other nine\nscreenshots are untouched, which is the set CI reported failing.","tree":{"sha":"ce38bd6420099280b25c61819ce42b30475297e3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OHDSI/Atlas3/git/trees/ce38bd6420099280b25c61819ce42b30475297e3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OHDSI/Atlas3/git/commits/8899614615e426b99185a2e4527ecb72104c1db2","verification":{"payload":"tree ce38bd6420099280b25c61819ce42b30475297e3\nparent d0021bf985528a371b8fbe34da6da20de8b2e0a8\nauthor Peter Hoffmann <954078+p-hoffmann@users.noreply.github.com> 1786688413 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786688413 +0800\n\nMake the active tab clearly distinguishable in shared page tabs (#235)\n\n* Make the active tab clearly distinguishable in shared page tabs (#209)\n\nThe Search/Recommend tab selector (and every other page using the\nshared .page-tabs style) relied only on a 2px slider and a color shift\nto show which tab was active, easy to miss at a glance. Bump the\nselected tab''s weight and slider thickness.\n\n* Re-record the visual baselines the tab styling changes\n\nBumping the selected tab''s weight and slider thickness changes how every\npage carrying .page-tabs renders, so the committed screenshots for\ncharacterizations, concept sets, incidence rates and pathways no longer\nmatch.\n\nRe-recorded in mcr.microsoft.com/playwright:v1.61.1-noble, the same image\nthe e2e workflow runs, so the baselines match CI''s font rendering rather\nthan a host machine''s. Only the five tabbed pages changed; the other nine\nscreenshots are untouched, which is the set CI reported failing.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqfrOdCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAmf4QAKo+aLn4Cc3pm9KfrIoDaoR9\nmO3zA4zoaqSMXs+du1rdnjKXlm2cFpACAMkJLT4tJsUd2jAu8Xzj69nZrgNxOZ+d\nPMaPlt+IXrHQ7W76XRvlT7meC9pr2/CFpeVmGiWWgZg7R+a65XW9hZ74B04Hbeo5\ndS3H0rTrCpH+RjSCKnV+K0JRUiMvPVpXU1k6dYW8icB2TsyPIkkE+TmIS082ideY\nLXZY98LHZt5escNiL+Way+NgUSYgRB1Jne3vhbgE37D/r174OyStPchjvbBdhUo7\nnJ/joWlKwxT/Ek5kWB1NIR2nTVZFJMuRqNB4cE1De2ot9fJmmDACMVL9lqQAYsRK\n4S86VhqVNek0m+PkAiz+/39SQrSKeFRAYN4QXEswPZ2Fqce9Ai6WW1Eu9OP2Ljbq\nAjIug6X+RtKdfCH5pW4flNsfddqdwz+KS1eNzysSNZXaGZrVCIaQk04eH9NX3NVr\ndgE+313dtCyQwiph972eNYuei6Y1GnIZH6fWzpYFXXbtu20fpc3tVSzCpz3N+1RX\nhC0f85DaB/A5d21BOQf2+ahSijKzDaa1FqC1RQamusj9NiV9fWdIzQc0NFTrckit\n8Oy9fWRlY8c6CKhXjxFsjjCt51XwUZJe9zikwyZeG45Vj/+GML2ncDKQDO07csdn\nXMzgZTJho1XYl8XL4eCm\n=ZIoz\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-14T06:20:17Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/OHDSI/Atlas3/commit/8899614615e426b99185a2e4527ecb72104c1db2","node_id":"C_kwDOQWYjcNoAKDg4OTk2MTQ2MTVlNDI2Yjk5MTg1YTJlNDUyN2VjYjcyMTA0YzFkYjI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/OHDSI/Atlas3/commit/d0021bf985528a371b8fbe34da6da20de8b2e0a8","sha":"d0021bf985528a371b8fbe34da6da20de8b2e0a8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OHDSI/Atlas3/commits/d0021bf985528a371b8fbe34da6da20de8b2e0a8"}],"sha":"8899614615e426b99185a2e4527ecb72104c1db2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OHDSI/Atlas3/commits/8899614615e426b99185a2e4527ecb72104c1db2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/954078?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/p-hoffmann/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/p-hoffmann/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/p-hoffmann/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/p-hoffmann/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/p-hoffmann","id":954078,"login":"p-hoffmann","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk1NDA3OA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/p-hoffmann/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/p-hoffmann/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/p-hoffmann/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/p-hoffmann/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/p-hoffmann/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/p-hoffmann","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OHDSI/Atlas3/commits/d0021bf985528a371b8fbe34da6da20de8b2e0a8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-14T06:19:55Z","email":"954078+p-hoffmann@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Peter Hoffmann"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-14T06:19:55Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Fix Observation Length chart x-axis truncating fractional year labels (#208) (#234)\n\nThe histogram chart''s x-axis label formatter floored every tick to a\nwhole number. That is correct for integer bin sizes (age in years),\nbut Observation Length uses 30-day bins expressed as fractional years,\nso ticks like 1.25 and 2.5 were both floored to whole numbers,\nproducing duplicated labels (0, 1, 1, 2, 2...) instead of one-decimal\nvalues like the Cumulative Observation chart shows. Reuse the\ntooltip''s existing fractional-safe formatter for the axis labels too.","tree":{"sha":"c5361fabb56620aed667d1978d1a392ec8b21a85","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OHDSI/Atlas3/git/trees/c5361fabb56620aed667d1978d1a392ec8b21a85"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OHDSI/Atlas3/git/commits/d0021bf985528a371b8fbe34da6da20de8b2e0a8","verification":{"payload":"tree c5361fabb56620aed667d1978d1a392ec8b21a85\nparent c891e0e58bc15ffcc3af872d8022da73d268673c\nauthor Peter Hoffmann <954078+p-hoffmann@users.noreply.github.com> 1786688395 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786688395 +0800\n\nFix Observation Length chart x-axis truncating fractional year labels (#208) (#234)\n\nThe histogram chart''s x-axis label formatter floored every tick to a\nwhole number. That is correct for integer bin sizes (age in years),\nbut Observation Length uses 30-day bins expressed as fractional years,\nso ticks like 1.25 and 2.5 were both floored to whole numbers,\nproducing duplicated labels (0, 1, 1, 2, 2...) instead of one-decimal\nvalues like the Cumulative Observation chart shows. Reuse the\ntooltip''s existing fractional-safe formatter for the axis labels too.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqfrOLCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAbjQQAIV82gJJqGyK4mrOxcIEqjrq\nG/LBSWZOG8hPe0ZFHnHnCgmrBbSW5pkFX4CqeyTYAEfUINUjRoAAGc/QK6L6oL4Q\n4g7o9eQZ2iDkDmZuSWBPxUmVFQ2PrQFhtiBkiWsCIj4OjUDFT6NFhZv5LLLcGKr4\nPVQNA7cTyl/QaKe9N/3iFUL757mguBZofZxfKP870RbwyCNlmJAFXRDE68wXBrh4\nE811K1dj6S5iYBnf1WHaPuIJowL0zf3WXCP6/rw1T6UjEBdxvD05xXsX3X/KGN1G\nLXKTc5qAv3dHslT0YZjhHUaYr6Wx1VboHpgwi4x2g7QphhsPKGMQTIO3kTjXj8B3\nDAFLaUvQeBtlDMvuxx+j2nArEIVo0O2TO1uEGVtLRI5vyWLZ2/Jo5pT/9FUijT81\n0bisjmDsYt4D7MmOxs/ojdXKgbm0aGNMbhI5WviSZK9SkynCAHcqXAvwjcKHtyPr\nM+N16119KEaRQ6Pp5nH2oHDe44UX+9m1X6WR0crOYDtIB85QRaxbr8o4Srn5ksr+\nAcBZbbSn+Zfjz9Sm42acUs9XmZKY8HJ9V6+BYBIOa0805ruTmgcPp+oiwv3f/pxU\n75WFWEHDvk4wrRP0YvNtdC6G8PzcRPO9CHlsUXhrk+MAHIGeBzqDpliFTYZJZugn\nzUfTMIxDrjJ2cIK8uI44\n=U5QH\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-14T06:20:04Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/OHDSI/Atlas3/commit/d0021bf985528a371b8fbe34da6da20de8b2e0a8","node_id":"C_kwDOQWYjcNoAKGQwMDIxYmY5ODU1MjhhMzcxYjhmYmUzNGRhNmRhMjBkZThiMmUwYTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/OHDSI/Atlas3/commit/c891e0e58bc15ffcc3af872d8022da73d268673c","sha":"c891e0e58bc15ffcc3af872d8022da73d268673c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OHDSI/Atlas3/commits/c891e0e58bc15ffcc3af872d8022da73d268673c"}],"sha":"d0021bf985528a371b8fbe34da6da20de8b2e0a8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OHDSI/Atlas3/commits/d0021bf985528a371b8fbe34da6da20de8b2e0a8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/954078?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/p-hoffmann/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/p-hoffmann/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/p-hoffmann/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/p-hoffmann/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/p-hoffmann","id":954078,"login":"p-hoffmann","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk1NDA3OA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/p-hoffmann/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/p-hoffmann/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/p-hoffmann/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/p-hoffmann/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/p-hoffmann/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/p-hoffmann","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OHDSI/Atlas3/commits/c891e0e58bc15ffcc3af872d8022da73d268673c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-14T06:06:30Z","email":"954078+p-hoffmann@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Peter Hoffmann"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-14T06:06:30Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Fix concept set list showing used sets as unused, and the duplicate-looking validation warning (#233)\n\n* Fix concept set list showing used sets as unused (#205)\n\nextractConceptSets(), which powers the used/unused flag in the concept\nset list and the ConceptSets array sent for server-side validation,\nonly checked event.conceptSet directly on entry events, additional\ncriteria, inclusion rules, exit and censoring criteria. It never\nrecursed into nested/correlated criteria groups (event.nestedCriteria)\nor checked conceptSet-type attributes, unlike the sibling usage-update\nwalk in utils/concept-set-usages.ts, which already handles both. A\nconcept set referenced only through one of those paths was invisible\nto this scan and got flagged as unused even though it was genuinely in\nuse.\n\nRewrite extractConceptSets to mirror the same recursive walk.\n\n* Fix duplicate-looking concept set validation warning (#214)\n\nA freshly-added criterion is seeded with a placeholder concept set\nreference (id null, name ''Select concept set...'') rather than leaving\nconceptSet unset. extractConceptSets treated any object on\nevent.conceptSet as a real, used concept set, so the placeholder was\nfolded into the list sent for server-side validation. Downstream, the\nAtlas JSON converter falls back to the array index as a fabricated id\nfor any non-numeric id, which can collide with a real, already\nselected concept set''s actual id in the same payload, producing a\nsecond, confusing ''Select Concept Set...'' warning next to the\nlegitimate one.\n\nRequire a real, non-null id before counting a concept set reference as\nused.","tree":{"sha":"81a5c8d1d6789ec3158d24adea9685dcca9866df","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OHDSI/Atlas3/git/trees/81a5c8d1d6789ec3158d24adea9685dcca9866df"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OHDSI/Atlas3/git/commits/c891e0e58bc15ffcc3af872d8022da73d268673c","verification":{"payload":"tree 81a5c8d1d6789ec3158d24adea9685dcca9866df\nparent faf476c63b10d04efab29ca2e7436b5f70b1e22a\nauthor Peter Hoffmann <954078+p-hoffmann@users.noreply.github.com> 1786687590 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786687590 +0800\n\nFix concept set list showing used sets as unused, and the duplicate-looking validation warning (#233)\n\n* Fix concept set list showing used sets as unused (#205)\n\nextractConceptSets(), which powers the used/unused flag in the concept\nset list and the ConceptSets array sent for server-side validation,\nonly checked event.conceptSet directly on entry events, additional\ncriteria, inclusion rules, exit and censoring criteria. It never\nrecursed into nested/correlated criteria groups (event.nestedCriteria)\nor checked conceptSet-type attributes, unlike the sibling usage-update\nwalk in utils/concept-set-usages.ts, which already handles both. A\nconcept set referenced only through one of those paths was invisible\nto this scan and got flagged as unused even though it was genuinely in\nuse.\n\nRewrite extractConceptSets to mirror the same recursive walk.\n\n* Fix duplicate-looking concept set validation warning (#214)\n\nA freshly-added criterion is seeded with a placeholder concept set\nreference (id null, name ''Select concept set...'') rather than leaving\nconceptSet unset. extractConceptSets treated any object on\nevent.conceptSet as a real, used concept set, so the placeholder was\nfolded into the list sent for server-side validation. Downstream, the\nAtlas JSON converter falls back to the array index as a fabricated id\nfor any non-numeric id, which can collide with a real, already\nselected concept set''s actual id in the same payload, producing a\nsecond, confusing ''Select Concept Set...'' warning next to the\nlegitimate one.\n\nRequire a real, non-null id before counting a concept set reference as\nused.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqfrBmCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAADcoQAHLX1wK3dgcrvCNhJ54OdCyq\nHi8YMshdNj2wqV42j2M6v+eKIHbX68NCBYWyJrsuXh7hpUGWfbapPa4N+5OF9/Rv\nReJYA5frWg5FvKKATOIc0kfTf/jL5ysdICakPCZM+YnCrA9ev2dVt8uPaU1CA0kD\nwn1t1op9b9N9ulY/l6gp/8imkVP5PSdBHWUC4QDb99tmwMx23GtCLCH3wf28S9S/\nbzMid/cEGAHVZEzjGWRy3dajGsaIv4cequXs2uIeXAQi3Ad